<title>BRAZIL: Brazil senators insist CVRD proceeds go to states.</title>
<headline>Brazil senators insist CVRD proceeds go to states.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senators allied to the Brazilian government have told President Fernando Henrique Cardoso that proceeds from the sell-off of state mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce should go to the states, officials said.</p>
<p>Newspapers reported that the government leader in the Senate, Sen. Elcio Alvares, and the government's leader in Congress, Sen. Jose Roberto Arruda, had warned Cardoso this was the best way to thwart opposition attempts to scuttle the sale.</p>
<p>An aide to Arruda confirmed the reports.</p>
</text>
